    "insert": "\nOverall, the questions show a strong relation with the study's goals and are situated within the context of the current literature.\n\nThe use of \"Embodied Cognition Theory\" as the theoretical framework is a remarkable strength of this expose. It provides a solid basis for studying holographic AI, highlighting the critical role of physical and environmental interactions in cognition. The connection between this theory the proposed system is nicely put together, especially the argument that 3D interactivity can significantly improve both learning outcomes and task execution.\nIn order to strengthen this section more:-\nAdding a small example of how Embodied Cognition Theory has been applied in similar technological contexts to provide a support for the argument."
